{"turn": 6, "tool": "draft_summary", "args": {"provider_id": "1000000114"}, "result_chars": 2095, "result": "{\"provider\": \"1000000114\", \"summary\": {\"headline\": \"1000000114: 5 of 8 documented 99215 claims (62%) are documented below the billed level\", \"leaning\": \"pattern_consistent_with_upcoding\", \"rationale\": \"1000000114 billed 99215 on 25.4% of 690 claims against an expected 2.6% given patient complexity (risk-adjusted score 16.75; plain z-score vs peers 3.45). 58% of this provider's 99215 claims were on patients with 0 or 1 chronic conditions. Records came back for 30 claims. Of 8 documented 99215 claims, 5 (62%) were documented below the billed level, against 17% for the comparison providers. 1 of 17 notes claiming moderate-or-higher data reviewed had no lab or test line on the claim. This pattern is consistent with upcoding. It is a reason to review the records, not a finding. Examples: C0057808: billed 99215, patient aged 46 with 4 chronic condition(s) (type 2 diabetes;obesity;hypertension;asthma); documented MDM level moderate, 35 minutes. C0057937: billed 99215; documented MDM level moderate, minutes not recorded. C0057965: billed 99215, patient aged 53 with 1 chronic condition(s) (asthma); documented MDM level moderate, 30 minutes. C0057714: billed 99215, patient aged 26 with 0 chronic condition(s). C0057722: billed 99215, patient aged 39 with 1 chronic condition(s) (hyperlipidemia). C0057734: billed 99215, patient aged 36 with 0 chronic condition(s).\", \"cited_claim_ids\": [\"C0057808\", \"C0057937\", \"C0057965\", \"C0057714\", \"C0057722\", \"C0057734\"], \"next_steps\": [\"Request the full records for the cited claims and have a certified coder re-score each against current E/M documentation rules (medical decision making or total time).\", \"If the re-scoring confirms the pattern, use the sampling plan in the recovery packet to review a statistical sample of this provider's 99215 claims.\", \"Check whether notes for the cited claims loo